# Exclusion is modelled as PRESENCE OF A ROW, not a boolean flag, so the default state
# of every sample is "counted" and excluding something is an explicit, attributable act.
# Every flag the view emits is an *exclusion* signal (0 = count it), which means a
# missing dictionary key, a forgotten dictGetOrDefault, or a wrong default all resolve
